# Trivy Ignore File
# This file documents security vulnerabilities that are accepted risks or not applicable
# to this application. Each CVE is documented with justification.

# ============================================================================
# HIGH SEVERITY - System-Level CVEs (Not Application Code)
# ============================================================================

# CVE-2025-69720: ncurses buffer overflow in infocmp command
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability is in the `infocmp` command-line tool, not the ncurses library
#   - This application does not use or execute the infocmp tool
#   - The ncurses library functions used by Python are not affected
#   - Risk: LOW (tool not used by application)
#   - Mitigation: Run container as non-root user (UID 1000)
# Affected packages: libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-69720
CVE-2025-69720

# CVE-2026-29111: systemd IPC API arbitrary code execution
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability requires systemd running as PID 1
#   - Docker containers do not run systemd as PID 1
#   - This application uses Python as entrypoint, not systemd
#   - systemd libraries may be present but systemd daemon is not running
#   - Risk: LOW (systemd not running in container)
#   - Mitigation: Container does not run systemd process
# Affected packages: libsystemd0, libudev1
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-29111
CVE-2026-29111

# CVE-2026-4878: libcap TOCTOU race condition in cap_set_file()
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability requires write access to parent directory
#   - Requires specific race condition timing to exploit
#   - This application does not use file capabilities
#   - Application runs as non-root user with limited permissions
#   - Risk: LOW (feature not used, non-root container)
#   - Mitigation: Run as non-root user, read-only filesystem where possible
# Affected packages: libcap2
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4878
CVE-2026-4878

# ============================================================================
# MEDIUM SEVERITY - System-Level CVEs (Not Application Code)
# ============================================================================

# CVE-2026-4046: glibc iconv() DoS
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability in iconv() character set conversion function
#   - Python application does not directly call iconv()
#   - Risk: LOW (function not used by application)
# Affected packages: libc6
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4046
CVE-2026-4046

# CVE-2026-4437: glibc DNS response parsing
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability in DNS response parsing
#   - Application uses Python's high-level requests library, not direct glibc DNS calls
#   - Risk: LOW (vulnerable code path not directly exposed)
# Affected packages: libc6
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4437
CVE-2026-4437

# CVE-2026-4438: glibc gethostbyaddr hostname validation
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability in gethostbyaddr() function
#   - Python application uses modern DNS resolution, not deprecated gethostbyaddr
#   - Risk: LOW (function not used by application)
# Affected packages: libc6
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4438
CVE-2026-4438

# CVE-2026-5435: glibc TSIG record OOB write
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability in TSIG (DNS transaction signature) record processing
#   - Application does not process TSIG records
#   - Risk: LOW (feature not used)
# Affected packages: libc6
# References: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-5435
CVE-2026-5435

